# Dexed for WebCLAP

Dexed by Digital Suburban (Pascal Gauthier), a DX7 FM synthesizer, ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official Dexed release.

- Dexed: https://github.com/asb2m10/dexed (commit fea2f0f, version 1.1.0)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-dexed.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

## License

The bundle as a whole is licensed under the **GNU Affero General Public License, version 3** (`LICENSE`).

Dexed is GPL-3.0 (`licenses/GPL-3.0.txt`). Both modules contain the JUCE framework, used under the AGPL-3.0, so
`module.wasm` and `ui/ui.wasm` are AGPL-3.0. GPL-3.0 section 13 permits the combination.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied
warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licenses for details.

Dexed's FM engine (`msfa`) is Google's music-synthesizer-for-android (Apache-2.0); its OPL3 engine builds on Steffen
Ohrendorf's PPPlay implementation (GPL-3.0, as part of Dexed).

